=== narrow ===

 do one of everything so I can see what
 each call says about itself


One of each, then.

$ COUNT=0; for NAME in *.g… ✓ 2s 3L 700M
ls ✓ 2L
read diagram.png ✓ ~1.6Kt
edit screen.go ✓ +12 −5
grep ^func\\s+(N… ✓ 7L+ ~100t (of ~3.4Kt)
read README.md ✓ 3L

Here is a script, and a pattern beside
it:

for NAME in $(ls *.go); do
    COUNT=$(grep -c "func" "$NAME")
    echo "$NAME has $COUNT"
done

^\\s*(func|type)\\s+\\w{3,12}\\(

That is one call of every kind the
harness knows how to measure.
